WEBVTT

00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:14,770
A few weeks ago I was asking you about Resveratrol, you mentioned that it has a very short half-life,

00:00:14,770 --> 00:00:19,650
so it takes smaller doses throughout the day. I was wondering if that holds true for the

00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:27,490
fermented Resveratrol from Premier Research Lab. It's the same. Yes, so Premier Research Lab has

00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:35,410
kind of one of their things and a lot of their supplements are they are fermented in batch doses.

00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:42,690
I've actually toured their facility down in Austin, Texas, where they make these things quite interesting.

00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:53,570
And they have fermented Resveratrol. I have a lot of you people on the fermented tumeric.

00:00:53,570 --> 00:01:02,850
I think it adds to its benefits to the body. I think it adds to its accessibility as far as

00:01:02,850 --> 00:01:08,370
absorbability. So I think they're great products, but it doesn't shorten their half-life.

00:01:08,930 --> 00:01:15,250
So you'll still, the half-life is just how fast your body breaks down the end product in your

00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:20,610
tissues and in the blood. So it still has a very short half-life, so you still want to

00:01:22,370 --> 00:01:27,410
break it up through the day. And that's really goes through, goes for all of your supplements.

00:01:27,410 --> 00:01:31,970
The more you can split up your doses, let's say you're supposed to take three a day of something,

00:01:31,970 --> 00:01:39,010
and you take them all in the morning, that might not be the best way to dose things

00:01:40,050 --> 00:01:47,410
for most supplements. Now it's different with your fat-soluble vitamins, and it's different if you're

00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:56,530
trying to get up to a certain dose of vitamin C so that you have the antioxidant effects of the

00:01:56,530 --> 00:02:01,330
vitamin C. So vitamin D, you could take that all at once. You don't need to split that up. That'll

00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:06,690
store it in your body. That vitamin A will store it in your body. Vitamin E will store it in your

00:02:06,690 --> 00:02:13,650
body, but a lot of your herbs, they're going to have a half-life. A lot of all your bio-flavanoids are

00:02:13,650 --> 00:02:19,730
going to have a half-life that aren't, that isn't real long. So by splitting it up, you're going to give

00:02:19,730 --> 00:02:30,450
your body a better benefit in how you deal with that and how it helps you.

